  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\{1,2,3\\}$. The number of relations on $A$, containing $(1,2)$ and $(2,3)$, which are reflexive and transitive but not symmetric, is ______ -",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$R$ is reflexive $\\Rightarrow R$ have $(1,1),(2,2),(3,3)$\n$R$ is transitive\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\because(1,2),(23) \\in R \\quad \\therefore(1,3) \\in R \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad R_1=\\{(1,1),(2,2),(3,3),(1,2),(2,3),(1,3)\\}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nClearly $R_1$ is reflexive and transitive but not symmetric.\n\nSimilarly,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& R_2=\\{(1,1),(2,2),(3,3),(1,2),(2,3),(1,3),(3,2)\\} \\\\\n& R_3=\\{(1,1),(2,2),(3,3),(1,2),(2,3),(1,3),(2,1)\\}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nTherefore, 3 relations are possible",
    "image": null
  },
